
BLCEDIT 1.0    by Wayne Stewart
~~~~~~~~~~~

What is it? 

Well it is the Battle Lands Character Editor.


Why is it? 

Well, after I made the Unregistered Version into a handicapped
version of the registered version I decided to make a character editor
for the sysop to drop in his maintenance drawer. I didn't place it in
the main program because I didn't want to bog the sysop down with a lot
of menus if he wanted to just play the game. I also didn't want to force
him to play the game just to edit a character.


Why do you need it?

I have no idea. You might want to edit a friends character or your own.
However, since this works with both the registered and unregistered
Battle Lands I left some flags out of it. I know how tempting it is to
want to turn every "NO" into a "YES" and every little number to a bigger
one so I left out most of the things which might cause damage. Just
remember that the maximum number maps in the unregistered version is
6 and in the Registered version it is 14. However, unless you know that
placing a character into a certain X/Y coordinate won't put them in a
wall I suggest you don't move the characters around.


What to do?

Be really careful. Be reasonable as well. Some flags you change might
not have any effect at all since there could be a call in the game for
the consequence of an action the second it occurs. Example: If you
change the character level to 35 (41 is max) nothing will happen
accept the monsters the character fights will be really tough. All his
stats will remain the same as they were because they only change when he
reaches a level within the game itself and all the cals are executed.
Also some flags are not good to say "YES" to if they were "NO". Example:
saying "YES" to Armor Gotten will make the character exempt from finding
the really neat suit of armor because the program will assume he already
has it.


How to set up?

Put it in pfiles and adopt as an arexx pfile at a high access level so 
no one but you or your cosysops can mess around with people's characters.


Disclaimer:

This file is very useful if you can think of soemthing you want to
check out or test and don't like taking the steps to get there. However,
it is also very dangerous. You can cause continuous loops, characters
to simply load improperly thus rendering them useless. Whatever you
do is your sole business but don't blame me that your users are 
complaining about getting kicked out of the game because you did
something to their character.


